---
title: Chicken saltimbocca
servings: 4
tags: [italian, chicken, quick, weeknight]
cuisine: italian
source: Chicken Saltimbocca by PBS Food, https://www.pbs.org/food/recipes/chicken-saltimbocca
---

In a #shallow bowl{}, mix the @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup} with
@kosher salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}.

Lay one leaf of @sage{8%leaves}(4 whole, 4 minced) along each of the
@chicken breasts{4}(cutlets, 6 to 8 oz each). Wrap a slice of
@prosciutto{4%slices}(3 oz, thinly sliced) around the middle of each to hold the
sage, press flat with your palm, then dredge in the flour and shake off the
excess.

Heat 2 tsp of the @olive oil{4%tsp} in a #large nonstick skillet{} over
medium-high heat. Cook two cutlets ~{3%minutes} to ~{4%minutes} a side, until
golden and cooked through, and keep warm. Repeat with the rest of the oil and
cutlets.

Pour the @dry white wine{3/4%cup} and @chicken broth{1/3%cup}(reduced-sodium)
into the skillet and boil hard ~{2%minutes}, until reduced by three-quarters.

Take the pan off the heat and let it cool ~{1%minute}. Stir in the
@unsalted butter{1%tbsp}(cold) and the minced sage until the butter melts,
~{30%seconds}. Spoon over the chicken and serve straight away.
